ular incumbent in a blue state, and most raters still call the race Safe R while markets give Janoo only about 15%. The UNH poll showing Janoo ahead is a real warning sign, but it conflicts with the Braun survey, so the forecast lands modestly in Scott's favor with elevated uncertainty.", "watch": "Whether subsequent polls confirm the UNH finding that Janoo has genuinely closed the gap, or whether Scott's typical late-race strength reasserts itself.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Phil Scott (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Vermont's governor race pits four-term Republican incumbent Phil Scott against Democrat Amanda Janoo in a state that leans Democratic by double digits but has repeatedly reelected Scott by wide margins. The polling picture is unusually muddled: a late-September Braun Research survey shows Scott ahead by ten points among likely voters, while a UNH survey from the same period shows Janoo up six, the tightest position any pollster has found him in a decade. Earlier UNH polls had Scott comfortably ahead.\n\nExpert ratings still lean heavily toward Scott, with most outlets calling the race Safe or Solid R, and prediction markets give him roughly an 83-85% chance of another term. The forecast treats Scott as a modest favorite, reflecting his incumbency advantage and track record, while acknowledging that the newest polling shows a genuinely competitive race developing.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2101, "margin": -4.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0165, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0219, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -10.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2344, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2363, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2599, "margin": -4.0}]}